uld change some minds I  don't know maybe there's a potential for  this to be good if if you've reached out  and and put Democratic candidates in  front of a Fox News audience but this is  a primary this is a primary there's  plenty of time for them to do that when  we get to the actual general election  debates if the risk is Fox will do what  they did to me when I went on Fox they  give everybody this bad lighting they  make the room so hot that the candidates  are sweating and they make them look  uncomfortable and not good I I think  you're right and that's why Fox should  televise the general election debates  and then the Democratic candidate can  make their fate their case in front of  the Fox News audience I think it's the  right decision when it comes to the  primary debates not everybody gets the  broadcast rather to moderate a primary  debate Fox News is just one of the  places where there will not be a  Democratic primary debate and I think  that it's the absolute right decision I  have a cringe-worthy bit of audio and  video for you today Donald Trump called  Apple's CEO Tim Cook Tim Apple Tim Cook  is really well known in the business  world and Trump likes having business  people around the White House now a lot  of them can't stand Trump so for example  Elon Musk bailed out of participating on  some kind of business advisory panel for  Donald Trump other CEOs have also said I  just can't work with the guy but anyway  Donald Trump was able to get Tim Cook to  go to the White House for something  called the American work force policy  advisory board and he called him Tim  Apple and I'm gonna play the video for  you twice in a moment the first time I  saw the video I thought maybe I heard it  wrong or maybe Donald from Studdard or  anything other than Trump called the guy  Tim Apple but he did he called him Tim  Apple and the look on Tim Tim Cook's  face sort of says it all you will also  notice that Ivanka all  so seems to kind of like a slightly  perkupp who is for whatever reason there  as usual I don't know why she's there  Jared Kushner's they are unelected and  not confirmed by the Senate advisors but  okay they are there here is Donald Trump  referring to Tim Cook as Tim Apple we  appreciate it very much Jim Apple but we  appreciate it very much Tim Apple but  this is just the best and hilariously  this is this has happened before  once Donald Trump had some kind of event  with Lockheed Martin's CEO Marilyn  Hewson and he referred to her as Marilyn  Lockheed check it out we have some of  our great business leaders and leaders  period right behind me I may ask Marilyn  Lockheed the leading woman's business  executive in this country according to  many this is just the best of course  she's the leading business executive of  women's business executive in the  country according to many more people  who actually know her real name rather  than Marilyn Lockheed is it possible  that Trump thinks since his businesses  are all called Trump whatever that every  business is named after the person  that's running the business or something  like that there's a report that Bill  Microsoft is now refusing to even meet  with the president after this incident  and Mark Facebook Berg is going to have  to face really tough questions from  Trump at the White House very very soon  I read something that's kind of an  interesting take on this which is that  this is a either conscious or  unconscious sort of psychological  domination game that Donald Trump is  playing that it is a way of showing that  he doesn't even need to call people by  the right name that to him they are  simply the CEO of the company  you're basically Tim Apple you're just  Tim the CEO of Apple you're Marilyn  Lockheed as he said it doesn't matter  what your actual last name is you're  just Marilyn the CEO of Lockheed Martin  it's an interesting  take but I think the more realistic  scenario is that this is part of the  cognitive decline that so many people  have been observing in Donald Trump in  which we will be following up on with a  psychiatrist dr. John Gartner very soon  sooner than then before you know it  John Gartner will be back on the program  we have a voicemail number that number  is two one nine two david p very  interesting voicemail about the criminal  justice system that came in take a  listen to this one hi David my name is  Lindsey I live in Tampa Florida I was  listening to your interview and was just  kind of wondering what the effects on  the criminal justice system will be if  all of those low-level offenders pled  not guilty what kind of effect would it  have on I mean the whole court system  from low-level misdemeanors all the way  up to high-level felonies but what you  get a salutely fantastic question  absolutely fantastic question  the criminal justice system the court  system would grind to a halt if they  lost the benefit of what I call the plea  deal industrial complex where most  charges do not lead to trials and it is  something that I've read sort of  extensively about if you actually were  able to get the resources for a lot of  these defendants and if the sort of  economic circumstances didn't prevent  them from just having to take a plea  deal and you got more not guilty pleas  it would grind the system to a halt in  such a an acute way that there would be  no choice but to reform the system and  to change how it functions but  unfortunately it all benefits from the  fact that a lot of defendants don't have  the financial resources to do it and  that for other reasons it's also  extraordinarily difficult but very very  good question we've got a tremendous  bonus show for you today we will talk  about a house democratic investigation  into voter suppression in Florida we've  been calling for this since the midterm  election and  is actually starting up the citizenship  question has been blocked from the 2020  census that's good news and we will talk  about it and lastly uber has been found  not criminally liable in the death of  the woman who was hit by a self-driving  car which we reported on extensively up  until this point that is according to a  prosecutor and we will talk about all of  those stories and more on today's bonus  show speak to you them  the david pakman show at david  pakman.com  [Music]  you
 

